    "introduction": "This guide will teach you how to replace the metal needle plate on the Brother CS6000i. You will need a Phillips #2 screwdriver as well as a 4mm flathead screwdriver. It will take about 15-20 minutes.",
    "what_you_need": {
        "tools": [
            {
                "text": "Phillips #2 Screwdriver",
                "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/products/6-in-1-screwdriver",
                "image": "https://cart-products.cdn.ifixit.com/cart-products/LYcK13TjejldWD5Y.thumbnail",
                "price": "$6.99"
            },
            {
                "text": "Flathead 4 mm Screwdriver",
                "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/products/flathead-4-mm-screwdriver",
                "image": "https://cart-products.cdn.ifixit.com/cart-products/6PhKONVIKrNmcGur.thumbnail",
                "price": "$5.49"
            }
        ]
    },
    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "title": "Body",
            "text": "Remove the five 20 mm Phillips #2 screws on the back of the device.\nRemove the single 28 mm Phillips #2 screw on the back of the device.\nRemove the single 23 mm Phillips #2 screw on the back of the device.",
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/gHBCqmQxl1xlTgNJ.medium",
            "image_links": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/gHBCqmQxl1xlTgNJ.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/4brVwmOqhKKA2aEh.200x150"
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/179996/384127",
            "comment_links": [],
            "additional_images": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/4brVwmOqhKKA2aEh.medium"
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Pull the white cover off.",
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/khTF4unDjLUHG6BN.medium",
            "image_links": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/khTF4unDjLUHG6BN.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/2bMLWSYLw5hesvYu.200x150"
            ],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/179996/384130",
            "comment_links": [],
            "additional_images": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/2bMLWSYLw5hesvYu.medium"
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Remove the final screw, a 11 mm Phillips #2.\nAfter removing all eight screws, you will have five 2 mm screws, one 28 mm screw, one 23 mm screw, and one 11 mm screw, all of which are Phillips #2.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/179996/384131",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "title": "",
            "text": "Slightly pull apart the two halves of the machine, taking care not to strain the attached cables.\nUnhook the white wires that are connected to the motherboard.\nFully separate the two halves.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/179996/384133",
            "comment_links": []
        },
        {
            "step_number": 5,
            "title": "Needle Plate",
            "text": "Remove the two screws securing the needle plate with a 4mm flathead screwdriver.",
            "image_links": [],
            "edit_link": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/179996/384329",
            "comment_links": []
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": {
        "text": "To reassemble your device, follow these instructions in reverse order.",
        "author_points": 30,
